    <item>
      <title>Trump Rejoiced in the Market’s Nvidia Surge. It Didn’t Last Long.</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/25/us/politics/trump-nvidia-stock-market.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/25/us/politics/trump-nvidia-stock-market.html</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:53:20 +0000</pubDate>
      <enclosure url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/25/multimedia/25dc-trump-econ-zmgl/25dc-trump-econ-zmgl-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg" />
      <media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/25/multimedia/25dc-trump-econ-zmgl/25dc-trump-econ-zmgl-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" medium="image" />
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/25/multimedia/25dc-trump-econ-zmgl/25dc-trump-econ-zmgl-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;margin-bottom:10px;" alt="Trump Rejoiced in the Market’s Nvidia Surge. It Didn’t Last Long." /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The retreat of the stock market in recent days shows how President Trump’s push to reinstall the company’s chief executive has collided with the realities of his other policies.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
